[7.22, "o", "Claude\r\n"]
[7.52, "o", "  ARC Prize 2026 - ARC-AGI-3 (per the Kaggle\r\n  competition pages, fetched today,\r\n  2026-10-02):\r\n"]
[7.82, "o", "\r\n  Deadline\r\n  - Final submission: November 2, 2026, 23:59\r\n"]
[8.12, "o", "    UTC (about 31 days from now).\r\n  - Entry and team merger: October 26, 2026.\r\n    You must accept the rules by then to\r\n"]
[8.42, "o", "    compete. The Timeline page says deadlines\r\n    are 11:59 PM UTC, but the competition\r\n    metadata shows entry closing at 11:59 UTC,\r\n"]
[8.72, "o", "    so accept the rules well before that day.\r\n  - Winners are announced December 4, 2026.\r\n    Both optional milestone deadlines (June 30\r\n"]
[9.02, "o", "    and September 30) have passed.\r\n\r\n  Metric: \"ARC-AGI-3 Metric\" (custom)\r\n"]
[9.32, "o", "  - Each game is scored from 0 to 100%.\r\n  - 100% means human-level performance: the\r\n    agent beat every game using the same\r\n"]
[9.62, "o", "    number of actions humans took.\r\n  - Using fewer actions than humans does not\r\n    score above 100%; scores are capped there.\r\n"]
[9.92, "o", "  - The final score \"averages individual game\r\n    scores across levels\", in the Evaluation\r\n    page's wording.\r\n"]
[10.22, "o", "  - The full methodology is at\r\n    https://docs.arcprize.org/methodology.\r\n\r\n"]
[10.52, "o", "  This is a code competition: you submit a\r\n  notebook, limited to 1 submission a day, and\r\n  the submission file is generated\r\n"]
[10.82, "o", "  automatically once the agent acts on any\r\n  game.\r\n"]
